Package: vantage
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 vantage-core (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Lightweight raw-C desktop environment
 Vantage is a lightweight Linux desktop environment written primarily in C,
 inspired by XFCE but implemented from scratch. It supports native Wayland,
 Xorg, and XLibre backends, hardware-accelerated rendering (NVIDIA/AMD/Intel),
 live video wallpapers, cross-toolkit Qt6/GTK theming, and runs without D-Bus
 or systemd if they are not available.
 .
 This package contains the desktop session binaries.

Package: vantage-core
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Core libraries for Vantage
 Internal libraries used by Vantage: vt-core, vt-config, vt-ipc, vt-renderer,
 vt-gpu, vt-backends, vt-compositor, vt-wm, vt-input, vt-session, vt-theme,
 vt-wallpaper, vt-desktop, vt-panel, vt-settings, vt-integrations.

Package: vantage-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: vantage-core (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for Vantage
 Headers and pkg-config files for plugin development.
